From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:35:38 -0400
Subject: Do not reset ext-idle-notify notifications when the inhibit state is
 unchanged

Bug: CIdleNotifyProtocol::setInhibit() (src/protocols/IdleNotify.cpp) calls update(0) on every
inhibitor-obeying ext_idle_notification each time it is invoked, whether or not `inhibited`
differs from the current state. update(0) reset()s the notification (sending `resumed` if it
was idled) and restarts its timer from zero. setInhibit() is reached from
CInputManager::recheckIdleInhibitorStatus(), which runs on every window focus change
(CFocusState::rawWindowFocus) and always ends in setInhibit(false) when no inhibitor is
active. Result: any focus change while the desktop is idle counts as user activity for
every ext-idle-notify client, even though no input happened and no inhibitor appeared or
went away. hypridle's shorter rules keep firing and its longer rules are never reached.

On this machine (2026-09-17 incident, docs/incidents/2026-09-17-idle-loop-no-suspend.md):
hypridle's 300 s DPMS-off rule fired 85 times overnight and got `resumed` 7-8 s later every
time. The HP 22cwa (HDMI-A-1) drops HPD ~6.5 s after losing signal; the wl_output removal
made fred.workspaces re-anchor focus (hyprctl --batch of focus dispatches), each of which
re-evaluated the (unchanged, false) inhibit state and reset the timers. The 1800 s
suspend-then-hibernate rule never ran; the machine stayed up all night.

Fix: return early from setInhibit() when the state is unchanged. A real transition still
restarts timers: true -> false is the spec's "inhibitor went away, start counting" and
false -> true still resets idled notifications. Only the no-op re-evaluation stops being
treated as activity. Hardware input still goes through onActivity() (PointerManager /
InputManager), which is untouched. A DEBUG log line marks the skipped case so the binary
can be checked for the patch (strings /usr/bin/Hyprland | grep 'inhibit state unchanged').

Upstream: same code on hyprwm/Hyprland main as of 2026-09-17 (fetched raw file). PR draft
in upstream-pr.md next to this file.

Retires when: an Arch hyprland release whose setInhibit() guards the unchanged case.
Packaged locally as 0.56.2-3.2 together with hyprland-dpms-off-on-connect.patch; any
Arch pkgrel or pkgver bump outranks it automatically (the pacman hook then says whether
to rebase or retire).

diff -ruN a/src/protocols/IdleNotify.cpp b/src/protocols/IdleNotify.cpp

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

